on of antidepressant medications</article-title><source>J Clin Psychiatry</source><volume>60</volume><issue>Suppl 4</issue><fpage>4</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10086478</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ndt-3-59"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gelenberg</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lydiard</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudolph</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Efficacy of venlafaxine extended-release capsules in nondepressed outpatients with generalized anxiety disorder: A 6-month randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>283</volume><fpage>3082</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10865302</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ndt-3-59"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gitlin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Venlafaxine, monoamine oxidase inhibitors, and the serotonin syndrome</article-title><source>J Clin Psychopharmacol</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>66</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9004070</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ndt-3-59"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greenberg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sisitsky</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kessler</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>The economic burden of anxiety disorders in the 1990s</article-title><source>J Clin Psychiatry</source><volume>60</volume><fpage>427</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10453795</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ndt-3-59"><citation citation-type="book"><article-title>Guidelines for the treatment of anxiety disorders in primary care</article-title><year>2000</year><publisher-loc>Toronto</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Queen&#x02019;s Printer of Ontario</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b19-ndt-3-59"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hodgman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Krenzelok</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Serotonin syndrome due to venlafaxine and maintenance tranylcypromine therapy</article-title><source>Hum Exp Toxicol</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>14</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9023570</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ndt-3-59"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoehn-Saric</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>McLeod</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hipsley</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Effects of fluvoxamine on panic disorder</article-title><source>J Clin Psychopharmacol</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>321</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8227490</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ndt-3-59"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynolds</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Alexopoulos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Hackett</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Venlafaxine ER as a treatment for generalized anxiety disorder in older adults: Pooled analysis of five randomized placebo-controlled clinical trials</article-title><source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><volume>50</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-